# Teacher-Facing Learning Records (Evaluations) — Summary

## 1. Teacher’s View of Learning Records

### Main page: `LearningRecordsPage.vue`

**Path:** `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue`

Teachers use this page for learning records. From `App.vue`:
- Teachers see nav items: 學習評量表, 我的課表, 帳號設定
- Default screen for teachers is `active = 'learning'` (LearningRecordsPage)

```129:129:frontend/src/App.vue
      <LearningRecordsPage v-if="active === 'learning'" :branch-id="currentBranch" :user-role="role" :user-id="session.user.id" />
```

### Secondary (unused): `TeacherEvaluation.vue`

**Path:** `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/TeacherEvaluation.vue`

- Designed for filling evaluations for a specific schedule (prop `scheduleId`)
- Not imported anywhere
- Teachers only use LearningRecordsPage to add records

### Director only: `DirectorDashboard.vue`

**Path:** `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/DirectorDashboard.vue`

- Shows pending evaluations for directors to approve
- Not teacher-facing

---

## 2. Per-file details

### LearningRecordsPage.vue

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **API usage** | `GET /api/v1/learning-records?branch_id=...&student_name=...&teacher_id=...&status=...` |
| **Teacher filtering** | Backend: `LearningRecordController` filters by `TeacherID` for `role === 'teacher'`. Frontend: teacher filter dropdown is hidden (`v-if="isDirectorOrSuperAdmin"`) |
| **Responsive CSS** | Media queries at 768px and 480px |

**API calls (lines 428–437):**

```428:437:frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
    const params = new URLSearchParams();
    if (filters.student_name) params.set('student_name', filters.student_name);
    if (filters.teacher_id) params.set('teacher_id', filters.teacher_id);
    if (filters.status) params.set('status', filters.status);
    if (props.branchId != null && props.branchId !== '') params.set('branch_id', String(props.branchId));

    const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/learning-records?${params.toString()}`, {
      headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}` }
    });
```

**Responsive styles (lines 853–892):**

```853:892:frontend/src/pages/LearningRecordsPage.vue
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .lr-filters-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .lr-form-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .lr-modal {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100vw;
    max-height: 100vh;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .lr-header {
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .lr-header button {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .lr-table-scroll {
    font-size: 13px;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .lr-form {
    padding: 16px;
  }

  .lr-modal-header {
    padding: 16px;
  }
}
```

**Issues:**
- Table has `overflow-x: auto` but no specific mobile layout; wide table may require horizontal scroll
- No card/list layout for small screens

---

### TeacherEvaluation.vue

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **API usage** | `POST /api/v1/learning-records`, loads schedule via Supabase `schedules` |
| **Teacher filtering** | N/A (per-schedule, `schedule.teacher_id` used) |
| **Responsive CSS** | `info-grid` is `grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr` only; no media queries |

**Issues:**
- Unused component
- Fixed 3-column grid on small screens would be cramped
- No mobile styles

---

### DirectorDashboard.vue

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **API usage** | `GET /api/v1/learning-records?status=pending,changes_requested&branch_id=...` |
| **Teacher filtering** | N/A (shows all pending for the branch) |
| **Responsive CSS** | No media queries |

**Layout:** `.dashboard-columns` uses `grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr)` (lines 468–471).

**Issues:**
- No breakpoints; 3-column layout will not stack on small screens
- `.stats-grid` is `repeat(4, 1fr)` (4 stats in a row)
- `.simple-table` has no responsive rules
- Likely horizontal overflow on phones

---

## 3. App.vue & Layout

### Navigation / sidebar

**Path:** `/home/admin/frontend/src/App.vue`

- Sidebar styles live in `/home/admin/frontend/src/styles.css`
- At `max-width: 900px`:
  - `--sidebar-w: 60px` (collapsed)
  - Brand text, nav labels, user name/role, branch switcher hidden
  - Only icons remain
  - `main-content` padding `20px 16px`

```848:874:frontend/src/styles.css
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  :root {
    --sidebar-w: 60px;
  }

  .sidebar-brand h1,
  .sidebar-brand .brand-sub,
  .brand-logo-container,
  .sidebar-nav button span:not(.nav-icon),
  .sidebar-footer .user-name,
  .sidebar-footer .user-role,
  .sidebar-footer .branch-switcher {
    display: none;
  }

  .sidebar-nav button {
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 14px 0;
  }

  .sidebar-footer .user-block {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .main-content {
    padding: 20px 16px;
  }
}
```

- `mobile-branch-bar` shows at 900px for branch selection when sidebar branch switcher is hidden

### Viewport meta tag

**Path:** `/home/admin/frontend/index.html`

```5:5:frontend/index.html
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
```

Correct for mobile viewport scaling.

### Global responsive CSS

- Main responsive logic in `/home/admin/frontend/src/styles.css` (sidebar at 900px, mobile branch bar)
- No global breakpoints for tables or other components

---

## 4. DirectorDashboard.vue — Mobile Responsiveness

- No `@media` rules
- Fixed layouts:
  - `.stats-grid`: 4 columns
  - `.dashboard-columns`: 3 columns
- Tables and review cards have no breakpoint handling
- `.column` has `max-height: 600px` and `overflow-y: auto`, but no width constraints for narrow viewports

---

## Summary of Issues

| File | Issue |
|------|-------|
| **DirectorDashboard.vue** | No media queries; 3-column dashboard and 4-column stats stay fixed on small screens; likely overflow |
| **LearningRecordsPage.vue** | Table only scrolls horizontally; no card layout for mobile |
| **TeacherEvaluation.vue** | Unused; 3-column `info-grid` has no mobile breakpoints |
| **SmartCalendar.vue** | No media queries for week/day/teacher views |
| **App.vue / styles.css** | Sidebar and branch bar responsive; no further global breakpoints |

Backend teacher filtering is:

```21:27:backend/app/Http/Controllers/LearningRecordController.php
        if ($role === 'teacher') {
            $teacherId = $request->attributes->get('auth_teacher_id');
            if (!$teacherId) {
                return response()->json(['message' => 'Teacher not linked'], 403);
            }
            $query->where('TeacherID', $teacherId);
        }
```
